  "scenario_text": "# Experiment G - hybrid fallback across simulated environments (RQ4 / H3).\n# The primary inventory replica (aws-simulated, 40 ms link) hangs from t = 10 s to t = 20 s of a 40 s\n# measurement. The secondary is in gcp-simulated (60 ms link). Pricing: azure-simulated, 30 ms.\n#   no-fallback        timeout 800 ms, no fallback\n#   fallback           timeout 800 ms, then the secondary (pays timeout + the longer link)\n#   fallback-breaker   + circuit breaker (5 failures, 5 s reset): skips the primary while open\n# Both \"failure domains\" are labels on one Docker host: this tests routing logic only.\nid: G_hybrid_fallback\ntitle: \"G - Fallback to a replica in another simulated environment\"\nhypotheses: [H3]\nrequires_mode: simulated\nworkload: {rate_rps: 20, arrival: poisson, warmup_s: 5, duration_s: 40}\nruns: 3\nseed: 707\ndefaults:\n  call_mode: parallel\n  resilience: {timeout_ms: 800, retries: 0, circuit_breaker: {enabled: false}}\n  links:\n    local--aws-simulated: 40\n    local--gcp-simulated: 60\n    local--azure-simulated: 30\n    aws-simulated--azure-simulated: 0\n    aws-simulated--gcp-simulated: 0\n    azure-simulated--gcp-simulated: 0\nconditions:\n  - name: no-fallback\n    resilience: {fallback: false}\n    faults: [{target: inventory-a, mode: hang, at_s: 10, duration_s: 10}]\n  - name: fallback\n    resilience: {fallback: true}\n    faults: [{target: inventory-a, mode: hang, at_s: 10, duration_s: 10}]\n  - name: fallback-breaker\n    resilience: {fallback: true, circuit_breaker: {enabled: true, consecutive_failures: 5, reset_timeout_ms: 5000}}\n    faults: [{target: inventory-a, mode: hang, at_s: 10, duration_s: 10}]\n",
